UID:dept-www-law-cam-ac-uk-events-3vb-university-cambridge-event@cambridge-
 events
DTSTAMP:20261122T190013Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20261126T170000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20261126T180000
SUMMARY:3VB University of Cambridge Event
LOCATION:Downing College
URL:https://www.law.cam.ac.uk/events/3vb-university-cambridge-event
CATEGORIES:Law,International
DESCRIPTION:Faculty of Law\nHighlight: Senior figure speaking (KC)\nTopics:
  Law\, International\nDetails: https://www.law.cam.ac.uk/events/3vb-univer
 sity-cambridge-event\nSign-up needed\nDate/time: \n\n Thursday 26 November
  2026 \n\n 5:00pm to 6:00pm\n\n Location: \n\n Downing College\n\n West Lo
 dge & Maitland Room\n\n About \n\n Following a brief introduction by 3VB's
  Rajesh Pillai KC\, members of 3VB will offer first-hand insights into two
  recent landmark cases\, exploring how legal decisions are reached and the
  role of barristers in shaping them.\n Dominic Kennelly will discuss Spain
  v Infrastructure Services Luxembourg [2026] UKSC 9\, concerning state imm
 unity and the enforcement of international arbitration awards\, while Will
 iam Day and Amelia-Rose Edwards will explore Gatwick Investment Ltd v Libe
 rty Mutual Insurance Europe SE [2026] UKSC 14\, addressing contractual int
 erpretation and causation in private law.\n The talks will be followed by 
 drinks\, refreshments and an opportunity to network with members of Chambe
 rs.\n RSVP: events@3vb.com \n\n Contact \n\n Email: events@3vb.com
END:VEVENT
